  "claim": "Across 100 crashes injected at every phase of a write, programs resumed on another node with no repeated writes (the 95% upper bound on the duplicate rate is 3.0%). The median resume took about 6 seconds, set by the lease timeout. Writes caught mid-flight are marked outcome unknown for a person to resolve. Under these settings, 0.0% of surviving nodes paused themselves for safety, and 0.0% of resumes missed the recovery deadline.",
  "honesty": "Two celld nodes, one object-storage provider (R2). Not durable execution / exactly-once. Columns: duplicates (safety), outcome_unknown (uncertainty), survivor self-fence/restart (availability), claim-path completed + stepsRepeated, plus statePreserved (exact digest equality vs per-trial no-crash twin on outer phases) and waitApproval (separate FLEET_PHASED_AWAIT_TRIALS arm). Denominators: see trialAccounting \u2014 no trials filtered; outer-only rates exclude mid-flight kills that intentionally end outcome_unknown. Completed reads are journaled and replayed; an interrupted read with no entry is re-requested once (resumption assumes that re-read is acceptable). Model calls: at most one repeated model request per crash, never a repeated write. Aggregate outcome_unknown \u2248 half only because kills are aimed evenly at four phases \u2014 two are the in-flight window; outer phases must stay 0 (nonzero = bug). Resume p50 \u2248 lease TTL + detection (failover floor).",
